message: "If you use this work, please cite the paper below."
title: "Exact Beyond Reach: What Gradient Descent Can and Cannot Change Around Frozen Structure"
abstract: >-
  Code, pre-registrations, results and paper. An LLM coding agent can write exact structure (wires, gates,
  bounds, switches) into a trained network's weights; this work asks what gradient descent does with such a
  frozen patch once training resumes. In 39 pre-registered experiments on a synthetic classifier, a
  super-resolution network, a cat GAN and Pythia-160M, the organising result is the reach law: a frozen
  patch fixes, exactly, everything beyond the reach of the trainable layers in front of it (attacks there
  moved the output by exactly 0.0 in all 39 models tested), and training renegotiates everything within
  that reach, including the patch's own boundary. Paper: https://v-code-895.github.io/exact-beyond-reach/
